Or the blessed +2 Grayswandir.  It'll blast a
neutral character, and Cavemen are restricted
in saber, but the artifact has a to-hit bonus,
(in addition to double damage and silver),
so even if restricted you can still use it.

Other artifact weapons that are good enough
to use even if restricted include Excalibur
(which grants particularly useful extrinsics),
Vorpal Blade (the damage bonus is not so
hot, but as a longsword it still does better
damage than many artifact weapons with
worse base types), and the Sceptre (but
that's your quest artifact, so not wishable).

Mjollnir and the Brands also qualify, but only
if you don't mind destroying monster inventory
and the fact that certain monsters are immune.
(IMO, carrying a weapon that's not so good
against foo-resistant monsters is basically
daring the RNG to send in a whole passel
of foo-resistant monsters at the worst
possible times.  Maybe your relationship
with the RNG is better than mine...)

There are also some two-handed ones that
qualify if you don't mind two-handed weapons.

Oh, and Stormbringer, but as far as I'm
concerned it's More Trouble Than It's Worth.
If you're wishing and not chaotic, there is
always a better choice, IMO.


